# Pre-commit secret scan (week 9, config hardening). One fingerprint per
# line, not a blanket file/path ignore — a *new*, different secret landing
# anywhere in .env.example still gets caught by gitleaks.
#
# .env.example:private-key:16 is the throwaway dev RSA keypair documented in
# that same file ("NEVER reuse this exact pair anywhere but a local
# machine") — intentionally committed so a reviewer can run the service
# locally without generating their own key first. Not a leak.
.env.example:private-key:16
